Ruby is a {{Rarity|Mythic}} [[Brawler]] who has moderate health, a long attack range, a variable damage output, immense utility with her Super, a fast reload speed, and a powerful synergy with [[Rey]]. She is the 110th/111th Brawler added to the game, alongside Rey. Her Trait allows her to heal and move faster towards an ally Rey when he is on the field. She attacks by throwing a club and a diamond card in a double helix formation, which deals more damage at the intersection. Her Super is an area that temporarily grounds and summons swirling projectiles in five directions, damaging any enemies in its path based on their maximum health. Her first Gadget, Shuffle and Cut, fires a projectile that splits that splits into smaller projectiles after hitting an enemy or reaching max range, healing allies and damaging any enemies in its path based on their maximum health. Her second Gadget, Stack the Deck, fires a stream of 4 suits in quick succession that knock enemies back and deal low damage. Her first Star Power, Lucky Number, increases the number of swirling projectiles. Her second Star Power, Double or Nothing, deals additional damage after hitting a target when her attack hits at intersection. Her Hypercharge, All In!, makes her Super grow in size and spread out the curving projectiles. Enemies caught by the projectiles will shoot in a chain reaction.

== Trait ==
{{Quote|POWER COUPLE <br><br> Ruby's main attacks heal Rey for 800 health. She also moves 10% faster towards him}}When an ally Rey is on the field, Ruby gains the ability to heal him and will also move towards him faster, able to reach each other quickly if both are approaching each other.{{Trait|Ruby-Power Couple}}

== Attack: Draw Two ==
{{Quote|Ruby throws a Club and Diamond in a figure-eight pattern. Hitting with both simultaneously adds extra damage.}}Ruby throws a club and a diamond card that travel similar to [[Nani]]'s main attack but only with two projectiles and two intersection points. These projectiles can pierce enemies, and the places of intersection deals high damage.

== Super: Royal Flush ==
{{Quote|Ruby creates an area, lasting for 4 seconds, that grounds enemies. Swirling shots fill the area and deal 15% max health damage.}}Ruby creates an area that grounds enemies inside it, and summons swirling projectiles in five directions, lasting for 4 seconds. The Super deals damage to enemies equivalent to 15% of their max health.

== Gadgets ==
=== Shuffle and Cut ===
{{Quote|Ruby fires a suit that splits into 5. These projectiles heal teammates for 1600 and deal damage equal to 15% of an enemy's health.}}{{Gadget|1}}Ruby fires a projectile that splits into 5 when hitting an enemy or after it reaches max range, similar to the main attack of [[Penny]]'s or [[Gene]]'s. These projectiles heal allies and deals damage to enemies equivalent to 15% of their max health.

=== Stack the Deck ===
{{Quote|Ruby fires a stream of 4 bouncing suits that knock enemies back and deal 400 damage.}}Ruby fires a stream of 4 suits in quick succession that knocks enemies back and deal 400 damage. The attack can bounce off walls and increase range when it does.{{Gadget|2}}

== Star Powers ==
=== Lucky Number ===
{{Quote|Ruby’s Super fills the area with 7 projectiles.}}{{StarPower|1}}This Star Power increases the number of swirling projectiles from her Super from 5 to 7.

=== Double or Nothing ===
{{Quote|Main attacks that hit with both projectiles cause the enemy to lose 10% max health per sec for 1 sec.}}{{StarPower|2}}If Ruby hits the enemy Brawler with both her projectiles with her attack, it causes them to lose 10% of their max health per second for 1 second.

== Hypercharge: All In! ==
{{Quote|Ruby’s Super grows in size and causes enemies hit by the shots to explode, firing even more projectiles.}}{{Hypercharge}}When activated, Ruby's Super expands in size and spreads out the curving projectiles. Enemies caught by the projectiles will shoot in a chain reaction. 

== Tips ==

* With Royal Flush, you can deal high damage to high health brawlers, especially tanks.
* Aiming Stack the Deck to a wall can increase the range, which is very useful to enemies from afar.
* With Double or nothing, the damage can be very high when hit on a Tank brawler.
*
